WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.600 --> 00:00:09.456
Hi! This is the last unit of A1.1. Great!

2
00:00:09.856 --> 00:00:14.256
Today we review everything – like in the exam.

3
00:00:15.967 --> 00:00:22.071
In the exam you introduce yourself. There are six key words:

4
00:00:22.471 --> 00:00:26.127
Name: My name is Valentina.

5
00:00:26.527 --> 00:00:30.903
Age: I'm twenty-four.

6
00:00:31.303 --> 00:00:34.959
Country: I'm from Colombia.

7
00:00:35.359 --> 00:00:39.111
Home: I live in Medellín.

8
00:00:39.511 --> 00:00:44.151
Languages: I speak Spanish and a bit of German.

9
00:00:44.551 --> 00:00:47.919
Job: I'm an engineer.

10
00:00:49.633 --> 00:00:54.777
The most important rule: the verb is in position two.

11
00:00:55.177 --> 00:00:57.849
I live in Bogotá.

12
00:00:58.249 --> 00:01:01.617
On Saturday I play football.

13
00:01:02.017 --> 00:01:04.401
What do you like doing?

14
00:01:04.801 --> 00:01:09.705
In yes/no questions the verb comes first: Do you have time?

15
00:01:11.400 --> 00:01:16.760
The accusative once more. Here is the apple:

16
00:01:17.160 --> 00:01:19.904
The apple is red.

17
00:01:20.304 --> 00:01:22.376
And now:

18
00:01:22.776 --> 00:01:25.280
I eat the apple.

19
00:01:25.680 --> 00:01:31.856
Only der changes. Die, das and the plural stay the same.

20
00:01:33.567 --> 00:01:37.679
Listen: Mateo is taking the exam.

21
00:01:38.079 --> 00:01:40.439
What's your name?

22
00:01:40.839 --> 00:01:43.607
My name is Mateo Ríos.

23
00:01:44.007 --> 00:01:46.535
Where are you from?

24
00:01:46.935 --> 00:01:51.095
From Colombia. From Cali.

25
00:01:51.495 --> 00:01:54.215
What do you do?

26
00:01:54.615 --> 00:01:56.879
I'm a student.

27
00:01:58.567 --> 00:02:09.087
Now you! Introduce yourself: name, age, country, home, languages, job. Go!

28
00:02:22.800 --> 00:02:26.936
Great! Now you can:

29
00:02:27.336 --> 00:02:37.712
You can introduce yourself and know the key grammar. You're ready for A1.2. Congratulations!

30
00:02:38.112 --> 00:02:41.528
See you soon in A1.2!
